WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:52.880
<b>I Will Surpass You</b>

3
00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:53.430
I don't know that I've even heard of such a company.

4
00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:56.830
Are you sure it exists?

5
00:01:56.900 --> 00:02:01.270
We're just ordinary citizens of Alabasta, Mr. Marine.

6
00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:02.910
You wouldn't wanna
hurt good citizens

7
00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:04.470
just because there's a rebellion.

8
00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:08.850
Wait, Sergeant Major, they...!

9
00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:10.420
[TASHIGI]
Shut up!

10
00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:12.820
Why were you hesitating, Marine?

11
00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:15.260
If you wait for proof, you won't prevent anything.

12
00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:18.270
You should be able to tell
who the enemy is immediately!

13
00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:20.800
Yes! We're very
sorry, Sergeant!

14
00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:22.940
[TASHIGI]
We only have until 4:30.

15
00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:25.270
We're running out of time.

16
00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:29.120
The clock.

17
00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:30.650
[MISS FATHER'S DAY]
Ribbit, ribbit, ribbit.

18
00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:32.060
Hey, listen, Mr. 7.

19
00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:34.020
I think this is a very
important mission

20
00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:35.990
the boss has assigned to us.

21
00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:37.660
I think you're
absolutely correct

22
00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.800
about that, Miss Father's Day.

23
00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:40.960
And do you know what else?

24
00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:42.660
I bet we'll get big promotions

25
00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:44.830
for pulling this off successfully, ribbit, ribbit.

26
00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:46.970
[laughs]

27
00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:49.370
I do hope that that is
the planned reward.

28
00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:51.370
After all, this is quite
a difficult mission

29
00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:53.360
when you think about it,
Miss Father's Day.

30
00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:54.960
We're shooting a cannonball
into the crowd

31
00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:56.600
using such a big cannon!

32
00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:59.840
[laughing]

33
00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:01.940
So the reward should
be just as big!

34
00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:04.810
[laughing]

35
00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:07.610
[MISS FATHER'S DAY]
Ribbit!

36
00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:10.550
It's almost time
to go now, Mr. 7!

37
00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:15.460
We're ready to fire! Yeah!

38
00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:30.320
What is it you're saying?

39
00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:34.350
What is it that you think I do
not understand, Straw Hat?

40
00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:44.590
[LUFFY]
Gum-Gum...

41
00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:46.960
...Gatling!

42
00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:56.330
I don't think you understand.

43
00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.970
You're going to die here very soon.

44
00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:02.270
The poison from my hook has entered your wound.

45
00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:06.510
[CROCODILE]
Your body is probably becoming

46
00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:08.480
numb right now.

47
00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:12.610
It doesn't matter whether you win or lose this fight.

48
00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:15.020
Your body will still be
buried underneath the rubble

49
00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:17.020
when this temple collapses.

50
00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:19.420
[MR. 7]
Fifteen seconds until we shoot!

51
00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:22.480
[MISS FATHER'S DAY]
Cannon aimed at the center
of Palace Square,

52
00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:25.150
ribbit, ribbit.

53
00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:27.120
Fire!

54
00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:28.320
[MR. 7 laughing]

55
00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:30.990
Hey, Nami! What the hell is it
you're trying to do anyway?

56
00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:33.160
We really don't have time to play around!

57
00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:35.460
If we mess this up,
we're gonna die!

58
00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:36.340
Hey!

59
00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:37.540
Thanks, Usopp, but I
already know that!

60
00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:41.240
Now just shut up and stand there
quietly! I'm calculating.

61
00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:43.720
Maybe I would shut up if I had
any idea what was going on!

62
00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:45.480
Would you just explain
what the hell it is

63
00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:46.480
you're planning already?

64
00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:49.180
[NAMI]
Calm down!
You'll know soon enough!

65
00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:50.310
Are you ready?

66
00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:51.650
[MISS FATHER'S DAY]
Ribbit, ribbit, ribbit.

67
00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:55.130
Hey, listen Mr. 7. This is
a very special occasion.

68
00:04:55.130 --> 00:04:57.430
I think we should
do a countdown!

69
00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:59.270
[MR. 7]
That's a good plan,
Miss Father's Day.

70
00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:02.060
A good plan, a very good plan.
Sounds interesting.

71
00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:03.040
[MR. 7 laughs]

72
00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:05.340
Forecasting... a typhoon!

73
00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:09.280
[BOTH]
– Here we go! Countdown!
– Here we go! Countdown!

74
00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:13.500
Cyclone Tempo!

75
00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:14.640
What?

76
00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:16.970
But wait, Cyclone Tempo is
just a silly boomerang game

77
00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:18.980
to play at parties!

78
00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:21.380
Just head for the clock tower!

79
00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:26.450
[wheezes]

80
00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:35.290
[USOPP screaming]

81
00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:38.430
What the...? They're flying up?

82
00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:42.030
Chopper! Jump up to where
Sanji is, all right?

83
00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:43.100
[CHOPPER, VIVI]
– Huh?
– Huh?

84
00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:45.800
That's it? This is her big plan?

85
00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:47.700
To make it all the way up
there piggy back like this?

86
00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:51.420
Sanji, you know what to do,
right? We have to hurry!

87
00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:53.690
[SANJI]
I think I get the
idea, but it's risky.

88
00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:56.320
Well, I guess I just have to do it.

89
00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:58.530
It's too late to turn back at this point.

90
00:05:58.550 --> 00:05:59.580
Tony, let's do this!

91
00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:02.620
Okay, Vivi. Now just
hang on tightly!

92
00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:06.450
I see. That's what
they're doing.

93
00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:08.740
Chopper! Get on my right leg.

94
00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:10.140
[CHOPPER]
Right!

95
00:06:11.780 --> 00:06:14.100
[MR. 7. MISS FATHER'S DAY]
Eleven seconds!

96
00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:16.100
[SANJI]
Here they come, Zoro!

97
00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:18.010
[NAMI]
Good job so far!

98
00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:22.150
[ZORO]
So I just throw them
to the top of that tower.

99
00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:23.480
[BOTH]
– Ten!
– Ten!

100
00:06:23.510 --> 00:06:25.180
[CHOPPER]
Zoro!

101
00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:27.610
Yeah, I'm ready. Come on up.

102
00:06:27.640 --> 00:06:28.540
Not swords!

103
00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:31.210
It's the flat of the
blade, calm down!

104
00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:32.140
Get your footing.

105
00:06:32.170 --> 00:06:33.210
[CHOPPER]
Okay!

106
00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:34.380
[BOTH]
– Nine!
– Nine!

107
00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:36.810
[ZORO]
Careful! There's a
couple of weirdoes up there.

108
00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:40.150
Yes, I know them.

109
00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:40.520
Oops.

110
00:06:40.520 --> 00:06:42.550
[MR. 7]
Hello, Miss Wednesday.

111
00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:44.960
[MISS FATHER'S DAY]
Ribbit, ribbit, ribbit.

112
00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:46.590
I'd recognize that
little traitor

113
00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:49.430
to our company anywhere!

114
00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:50.660
They noticed!

115
00:06:50.730 --> 00:06:51.630
They did?!

116
00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:54.570
We're still in the air.
This is really bad!

117
00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:57.840
If they shoot at us, we're finished!

118
00:06:57.870 --> 00:06:59.500
[CROCODILE]
Whatever it is you really want

119
00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:01.600
can't be in this country.

120
00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:05.340
Aren't I right? You're fighting
for somebody else's goal now.

121
00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:07.670
And how can there be any
point in dying for that?

122
00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:09.900
If only you would just get rid of a friend or two,

123
00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:13.570
you could easily avoid so many
of these inconvenient problems.

124
00:07:13.610 --> 00:07:16.940
Loyalty is only for
idiots and weaklings.

125
00:07:17.010 --> 00:07:18.580
[LUFFY]
Like I said,

126
00:07:18.610 --> 00:07:22.950
you really don't understand anything, do you?

127
00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:24.620
Vivi...

128
00:07:25.690 --> 00:07:30.190
[LUFFY]
Vivi is always telling
people not to risk their lives,

129
00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:31.960
but she's the first
to lay down her life

130
00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:33.850
in order to save others.

131
00:07:33.910 --> 00:07:37.750
If we don't help her,
she'll die. You'll kill her.

132
00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:40.280
[CROCODILE]
You still don't get it.

133
00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:41.850
That's what makes
her such a burden.

134
00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:44.850
So why not ditch the princess
and save yourselves?

135
00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:47.590
Because none of us want Vivi to die!

136
00:07:47.620 --> 00:07:50.520
Helping each other is what friends do!

137
00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:52.520
And that's why none of
us will leave her behind

138
00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:54.260
or quit fighting you!

139
00:07:54.290 --> 00:07:57.260
As long as she doesn't give up
on her country, neither will we!

140
00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:01.660
Even if that means all the rest of you end up dead?

141
00:08:01.700 --> 00:08:05.300
If we die, we die.
That's all there is to it.

142
00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:07.500
Adjust Ribbit-Ribbit
Gun for attack!

143
00:08:07.540 --> 00:08:09.440
This is an unexpected catch.

144
00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:11.540
Adjusting Yellow Gun!

145
00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:12.330
[laughs]

146
00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:14.170
How nice. How nice.
This is good!

147
00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:16.140
They are the perfect prey for us!

148
00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:17.960
What do you think you bastards are doing,

149
00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:20.060
pointing your guns at Vivi?!

150
00:08:20.130 --> 00:08:22.130
This isn't good! The two
of them are a sniper team!

151
00:08:22.170 --> 00:08:23.140
[ZORO]
Chopper!

152
00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:24.580
I'll throw you guys up, anyway.

153
00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:25.920
It'll change the direction,

154
00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:27.460
but you need to
figure somethin' out!

155
00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:29.090
[CHOPPER]
Huh? What do I do?

156
00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:30.590
We have seven seconds!

157
00:08:30.590 --> 00:08:33.460
Just figure something out!

158
00:08:34.550 --> 00:08:38.860
[ZORO]
Chopper, Vivi! Are you
ready? I'm sendin' you up.

159
00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:41.330
Ready?

160
00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:43.070
Aim and fire!

161
00:08:44.570 --> 00:08:48.340
Our bullets are set to crash into each other!

162
00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:50.210
And then they're going to explode!

163
00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:52.080
[laughs]

164
00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:53.480
[ZORO groans]

165
00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:55.670
No!

166
00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:01.040
What an idiot!

167
00:09:01.070 --> 00:09:02.640
He's hit!

168
00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:05.060
[CHOPPER]
Are you ready, Vivi?

169
00:09:05.090 --> 00:09:07.860
[VIVI]
Just throw me with
all your strength, Tony!

170
00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:10.950
<b>5 Seconds Until Detonation</b>

171
00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:13.400
It's no use, ribbit, ribbit.

172
00:09:13.430 --> 00:09:14.130
Dodging.

173
00:09:14.140 --> 00:09:16.070
[BOTH]
– Aim and fire!
– Aim and fire!

174
00:09:16.140 --> 00:09:18.420
Who's that?

175
00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:19.690
Huh?

176
00:09:19.710 --> 00:09:22.330
<b>4 Seconds Until Detonation</b>

177
00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:26.230
[CHOPPER screams]

178
00:09:26.260 --> 00:09:27.900
Where'd Miss Wednesday go?

179
00:09:27.930 --> 00:09:30.400
Oh! What now?

180
00:09:32.930 --> 00:09:35.770
[VIVI]
Peacock String!

181
00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:37.440
[MR. 7]
Up there!

182
00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:39.390
<b>3 Seconds Until Detonation</b>

183
00:09:44.510 --> 00:09:48.880
[CROCODILE laughing]

184
00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:50.280
You can talk as
tough as you want

185
00:09:50.350 --> 00:09:52.450
and keep blathering on about
friendship if you like,

186
00:09:52.520 --> 00:09:55.960
but your body is still
freezing up on you.

187
00:09:56.020 --> 00:09:59.090
You look pathetic, Straw Hat.

188
00:10:01.900 --> 00:10:04.030
[yelling]

189
00:10:04.060 --> 00:10:05.930
[VIVI]
Slasher!

190
00:10:08.740 --> 00:10:10.740
Ribbit. Well, Princess.

191
00:10:10.770 --> 00:10:12.810
Looks like you missed us!

192
00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:17.430
<b>2 Seconds Until Detonation</b>

193
00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:19.080
[VIVI]
Run Back!

194
00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:24.790
[USOPP]
All right!

195
00:10:31.110 --> 00:10:33.530
<b>1 Second Until Detonation</b>

196
00:10:47.340 --> 00:10:49.410
[CHILDREN]
– Vivi!
– Vivi!

197
00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:52.150
[GATEKEEPER]
Hey! Out of here, you brats!

198
00:10:52.180 --> 00:10:54.250
Did you sneak in through the shortcut again?

199
00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:55.280
Gatekeeper!

200
00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:56.950
[CHILD C]
Run!

201
00:10:56.980 --> 00:10:59.150
[GATEKEEPER]
Would the two of you
please say something

202
00:10:59.180 --> 00:11:01.520
to the kids to keep them away?

203
00:11:01.580 --> 00:11:02.990
[PELL]
Hm?

204
00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:04.990
Sure.

205
00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:06.140
Vivi. Going somewhere?

206
00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:07.810
[VIVI]
Mh-hm. The secret base.

207
00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:12.020
Right. Well, you
have a good time.

208
00:11:13.990 --> 00:11:17.020
[CHAKA]
So, where did Princess Vivi go?

209
00:11:17.090 --> 00:11:18.090
[PELL]
Huh?

210
00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:20.960
Oh, I can't tell you.
It's a secret.

211
00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:22.100
[CHAKA chuckles]

212
00:11:22.130 --> 00:11:24.330
[CHAKA]
The clock tower, huh?

213
00:11:53.670 --> 00:11:56.010
It stopped, right?

214
00:12:15.150 --> 00:12:20.150
[ticking]

215
00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:25.010
Oh, hey, you're still alive.

216
00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:28.510
Yeah. What happened
with the cannon?

217
00:12:29.950 --> 00:12:31.720
[MARINE B]
What was that?

218
00:12:36.670 --> 00:12:38.210
What's the matter?

219
00:12:38.270 --> 00:12:40.280
Apparently, somethin's
gone wrong up there.

220
00:12:40.310 --> 00:12:43.150
It's Vivi. We still
haven't seen her.

221
00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:47.280
Oh, no. You guys!

222
00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:48.480
[NAMI]
What is it?

223
00:12:48.520 --> 00:12:50.190
The cannon ball has
a timing device.

224
00:12:50.220 --> 00:12:52.960
If we don't do something, it'll explode!

225
00:12:53.050 --> 00:12:56.720
[USOPP]
Ah! What did you say?!

226
00:12:58.720 --> 00:13:02.360
A time bomb? No.

227
00:13:02.390 --> 00:13:04.120
[CROCODILE chuckles]

228
00:13:04.190 --> 00:13:06.060
[CROCODILE]
I was very well prepared, Cobra.

229
00:13:06.090 --> 00:13:09.390
You have to be willing to admit that much, surely.

230
00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:11.490
The most successful
missions always account

231
00:13:11.530 --> 00:13:15.000
for unforeseen circumstances.

232
00:13:15.030 --> 00:13:16.400
In this case, for instance,

233
00:13:16.430 --> 00:13:19.030
even if something happens to the cannoneers,

234
00:13:19.070 --> 00:13:21.670
the cannon ball will
still explode on its own.

235
00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:26.210
The attack will only be delayed
by a few seconds or so.

236
00:13:26.210 --> 00:13:27.640
Of course, I did
originally want it

237
00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:30.350
to be shot into the
center of the Square,

238
00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:32.520
but the cannon ball is big
enough that it should do

239
00:13:32.550 --> 00:13:36.250
plenty of damage
from right where it is.

240
00:13:36.350 --> 00:13:39.390
[CROCODILE chuckles]

241
00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:43.030
[CROCODILE]
Stopping the rebellion.

242
00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:44.680
Saving the kingdom.

243
00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:49.750
All those worthless ideas you've clung to for so long.

244
00:13:49.820 --> 00:13:54.190
In the end, they just created more victims for me.

245
00:13:59.060 --> 00:14:01.430
[CROCODILE]
Let me tell you something.

246
00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:10.120
[CROCODILE]
You're never going
to save this country.

247
00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:14.460
Damn it. This isn't right!

248
00:14:14.490 --> 00:14:17.600
Stopping the cannoneers
should've stopped the attack!

249
00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:19.440
A timer?

250
00:14:19.510 --> 00:14:22.710
Considering its power, even if it explodes from up there,

251
00:14:22.740 --> 00:14:26.050
it'll still kill all the people
in the Square and the town.

252
00:14:26.100 --> 00:14:27.570
Then what's gonna happen now?!

253
00:14:29.150 --> 00:14:30.120
Oh, crap!

254
00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:31.660
Does this just mean it
was impossible all along

255
00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:34.890
for us to stop the explosion
from happening?

256
00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:41.100
[VIVI]
He made us spend all
this time looking for it!

257
00:14:41.130 --> 00:14:44.500
He even announced the attack
so we would do just that!

258
00:14:44.670 --> 00:14:46.010
Why?

259
00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:49.080
[VIVI crying]

260
00:14:49.110 --> 00:14:51.680
Just how far will Crocodile
insist on going

261
00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:55.020
to make fools of us all?

262
00:14:55.050 --> 00:14:57.380
It's not enough for him to
tear this country apart,

263
00:14:57.420 --> 00:15:00.350
he has to mock us
while he's doing it!

264
00:15:02.190 --> 00:15:06.860
[VIVI]
Crocodile!

265
00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:17.990
And that's why none
of us will leave her behind

266
00:15:18.060 --> 00:15:19.800
or quit fighting you.

267
00:15:19.830 --> 00:15:21.900
As long as she doesn't give up on her country,

268
00:15:21.930 --> 00:15:23.170
neither will we!

269
00:15:34.020 --> 00:15:35.720
[CROCODILE growls]

270
00:15:43.770 --> 00:15:45.030
[LUFFY]
You can't...

271
00:15:49.100 --> 00:15:50.670
...defeat me.

272
00:15:52.870 --> 00:15:54.440
[CROCODILE]
You finally manage to speak,

273
00:15:54.480 --> 00:15:57.940
and that's all you can come up with?

274
00:15:57.980 --> 00:16:00.480
I suppose it's an acceptable
bluff from a loser

275
00:16:00.510 --> 00:16:02.320
who's about to die.

276
00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:06.290
But of course, like any bluff, it's empty air.

277
00:16:10.220 --> 00:16:14.000
[LUFFY]
Except, I'm the man
who'll be King of the Pirates!

278
00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:16.720
[CROCODILE]
Listen up, you damn brat.

279
00:16:16.760 --> 00:16:19.390
If you really knew anything about this sea,

280
00:16:19.420 --> 00:16:22.060
you wouldn't make
such an idiotic statement.

281
00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:26.400
I told you before.

282
00:16:26.430 --> 00:16:28.800
There are thousands
of rookies just like you.

283
00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:32.070
Every one of them chasing
their naïve little dreams!

284
00:16:34.810 --> 00:16:36.680
The sooner you understand the true level

285
00:16:36.740 --> 00:16:38.580
of the grand line,

286
00:16:38.580 --> 00:16:41.280
the sooner you'll give up
on your foolish dreams!

287
00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:44.610
[LUFFY grunts]

288
00:16:58.120 --> 00:17:01.720
[LUFFY]
I'm the one
who's gonna beat you.

289
00:17:04.770 --> 00:17:05.870
Wait, was that...?

290
00:17:05.940 --> 00:17:08.300
Yeah, I think it's the bird man.

291
00:17:12.440 --> 00:17:13.810
[VIVI]
Pell?

292
00:17:13.840 --> 00:17:16.650
Wow, this place brings back so many memories.

293
00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:20.550
The Sand-Sand Clan's
super-secret base.

294
00:17:20.620 --> 00:17:21.780
Pell, listen to me...

295
00:17:21.820 --> 00:17:23.980
You certainly were a mischievous
little child, Princess Vivi.

296
00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:25.450
You gave us no end of trouble

297
00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:29.220
with all your pranks
and disappearances.

298
00:17:29.220 --> 00:17:30.190
[ROYAL SOLDIER A]
It's Vivi!

299
00:17:30.190 --> 00:17:34.260
What's she doing in the ammunition bunker?

300
00:17:34.290 --> 00:17:37.630
Hey! What happened?
What was that explosion?

301
00:17:37.750 --> 00:17:40.290
[coughing]

302
00:17:40.320 --> 00:17:42.290
Princess Vivi, how many
times have we told you

303
00:17:42.320 --> 00:17:43.760
not to go near the
ammunition bunker?

304
00:17:43.770 --> 00:17:45.770
You could get hurt!

305
00:17:45.770 --> 00:17:47.340
[VIVI]
Pell!

306
00:17:47.370 --> 00:17:48.670
[ROYAL SOLDIER B]
Sir!

307
00:17:49.640 --> 00:17:52.940
I was trying to make some fireworks, but I messed up.

308
00:17:52.980 --> 00:17:54.610
I know it's the
anniversary of the day

309
00:17:54.650 --> 00:17:56.950
you joined the army, Pell, so...

310
00:17:58.400 --> 00:17:59.500
[ROYAL SOLDIER C]
What are you doing?

311
00:17:59.570 --> 00:18:02.500
[PELL]
I've told you a hundred times!

312
00:18:02.570 --> 00:18:05.770
Never, ever come near here!

313
00:18:05.810 --> 00:18:07.740
[IGARAM]
Just what do you
think you're doing?

314
00:18:07.740 --> 00:18:09.580
How dare you touch the Princess!

315
00:18:09.610 --> 00:18:11.750
You're through! No
one dares hurt her!

316
00:18:11.780 --> 00:18:14.240
Hold on, Igaram.

317
00:18:14.240 --> 00:18:16.400
It's fine.

318
00:18:18.750 --> 00:18:21.320
[PELL]
It could've been much worse.

319
00:18:22.570 --> 00:18:24.740
What if you were killed?

320
00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:32.440
[VIVI]
Faster!

321
00:18:32.510 --> 00:18:35.610
And go higher! Higher!

322
00:18:35.680 --> 00:18:38.250
[PELL]
Vivi, I need you
to promise me something.

323
00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:39.780
Never tell the king about this.

324
00:18:39.850 --> 00:18:43.090
[giggling]

325
00:18:43.120 --> 00:18:45.460
He made it clear that I'm not supposed to do this.

326
00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:48.220
He told me to never to go
flying with you on my back.

327
00:18:48.260 --> 00:18:49.460
If you're scared, fine!

328
00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:52.530
But I'll never forgive
you if you stop!

329
00:18:52.540 --> 00:18:53.600
[VIVI giggles]

330
00:18:53.620 --> 00:18:56.190
[VIVI]
After all, didn't
you say you'd do anything

331
00:18:56.270 --> 00:18:58.580
I wanted you to?

332
00:18:58.610 --> 00:19:02.800
[giggling]

333
00:19:02.800 --> 00:19:03.870
[VIVI]
Hey, Pell?

334
00:19:05.180 --> 00:19:06.080
[PELL]
Yes?

335
00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:08.560
[VIVI]
You train for
battle every day. Why?

336
00:19:08.600 --> 00:19:09.660
[PELL]
Because I'm a guard.

337
00:19:09.730 --> 00:19:11.800
It's my duty to protect this country.

338
00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:13.800
I have to stay strong.

339
00:19:13.830 --> 00:19:15.760
So, who will you be fighting?

340
00:19:15.760 --> 00:19:18.170
Who?

341
00:19:18.200 --> 00:19:19.400
I don't know.

342
00:19:19.430 --> 00:19:22.170
But I don't fight. I protect.

343
00:19:22.170 --> 00:19:23.740
[VIVI]
They're different?

344
00:19:23.770 --> 00:19:26.040
[PELL]
They serve different purposes.

345
00:19:26.070 --> 00:19:29.340
[VIVI]
Hmm. I don't understand.

346
00:19:34.380 --> 00:19:37.350
I'm so proud that I've
been able to serve you

347
00:19:37.350 --> 00:19:39.590
all these years, Princess.

348
00:19:39.620 --> 00:19:43.020
Protecting the Nefertari family has been an honor.

349
00:19:56.200 --> 00:19:57.800
[inaudible]

350
00:20:05.540 --> 00:20:07.280
[PELL]
I am...

351
00:20:07.310 --> 00:20:10.180
...Alabasta's guardian deity.

352
00:20:15.390 --> 00:20:17.060
[PELL]
The Falcon!

353
00:20:18.860 --> 00:20:21.660
[PELL]
And I am sworn
to destroy the enemies

354
00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:23.730
of the royal family!

355
00:21:31.440 --> 00:21:32.770
He's gone.

356
00:21:36.280 --> 00:21:38.980
[NAMI]
He saved us all.

357
00:21:41.120 --> 00:21:44.390
[USOPP grunts]

358
00:21:44.450 --> 00:21:45.320
[CHOPPER gasps]

359
00:21:45.350 --> 00:21:47.290
[USOPP coughing]

360
00:21:59.400 --> 00:22:02.000
[USOPP]
This can't be happening!

361
00:22:09.480 --> 00:22:11.380
Stop it!

362
00:22:11.410 --> 00:22:13.010
All of you, are you out of your minds?

363
00:22:13.010 --> 00:22:14.010
[MARINE A]
Ma'am! No!

364
00:22:14.080 --> 00:22:14.980
[REBEL A yells]

365
00:22:15.010 --> 00:22:18.950
[SOLDIERS yelling]

366
00:22:22.620 --> 00:22:23.790
What the...?

367
00:22:26.260 --> 00:22:27.760
[SMOKER]
Tashigi.

368
00:22:27.850 --> 00:22:30.090
I need you to keep a
vigilant eye on this country

369
00:22:30.090 --> 00:22:32.760
and where it ends up.

370
00:22:32.760 --> 00:22:35.030
Whether it falls,
or whether it survives.

371
00:22:35.090 --> 00:22:37.260
The dawn of a brand-new
and historic age

372
00:22:37.260 --> 00:22:39.260
is on the horizon.

373
00:22:39.300 --> 00:22:43.300
[SOLDIERS yelling]

374
00:22:55.110 --> 00:22:56.150
[TASHIGI]
Madness.

375
00:22:57.450 --> 00:22:59.780
[TASHIGI]
Why aren't they stopping?

376
00:23:03.460 --> 00:23:04.260
Stop it!

377
00:23:04.010 --> 00:23:08.010
[VIVI]
Stop fighting! Please stop!

378
00:23:08.010 --> 00:23:09.060
Stop

379
00:23:09.060 --> 00:23:10.110
fighting!

380
00:23:11.020 --> 00:23:13.430
Please stop!

381
00:23:13.460 --> 00:23:16.660
Please stop fighting!

382
00:23:16.700 --> 00:23:18.460
Stop fighting!

383
00:23:18.500 --> 00:23:20.630
Stop it, please!

384
00:23:20.670 --> 00:23:22.600
Stop fighting!

385
00:23:22.630 --> 00:23:32.300
Please stop! Stop fighting!

386
00:23:32.340 --> 00:23:35.100
Please stop fighting!

387
00:23:35.100 --> 00:23:37.270
– Stop it!
[ZORO]
– Vivi.

388
00:23:37.860 --> 00:23:42.360
Please stop fighting! Stop it!

389
00:23:42.400 --> 00:23:45.600
Please stop the fighting!

390
00:23:45.630 --> 00:23:50.140
Stop! Please stop fighting!

391
00:23:52.200 --> 00:23:53.920
Please stop!

392
00:23:55.190 --> 00:23:56.290
You fool.

393
00:23:57.290 --> 00:23:58.390
You dopes!

394
00:23:58.430 --> 00:24:01.400
Why are you just standing there?
Get your rears in gear!

395
00:24:01.430 --> 00:24:05.300
It doesn't matter how, just stop the rebellion!

396
00:24:05.370 --> 00:24:07.270
We've got to keep
the casualties as low

397
00:24:07.300 --> 00:24:09.200
as we possibly can!

398
00:24:09.200 --> 00:24:13.940
[crying]

399
00:24:13.980 --> 00:24:15.780
[VIVI]
Stop!

400
00:24:15.810 --> 00:24:17.210
Stop it!

401
00:24:20.150 --> 00:24:25.250
Stop fighting! Stop fighting!
Stop fighting!

402
00:24:25.290 --> 00:24:26.990
Please stop fighting!

403
00:25:18.400 --> 00:25:22.240
[CROCODILE]
The scorpion's poison
should be working by now.

404
00:25:24.400 --> 00:25:27.810
Where does this brat
get his strength from?

405
00:25:36.450 --> 00:25:38.990
[CROCODILE]
Mr. 5's team was taken down?

406
00:25:39.020 --> 00:25:40.460
Who the hell did it?

407
00:25:42.490 --> 00:25:44.490
Monkey D. Luffy?

408
00:25:44.530 --> 00:25:46.530
Never heard of him.

409
00:25:46.590 --> 00:25:48.860
Huh. It must be a mistake.

410
00:25:49.560 --> 00:25:51.760
You're saying that they're still alive?

411
00:25:52.100 --> 00:25:53.770
We've just received word.

412
00:25:53.810 --> 00:25:55.140
Those pirates have arrived.

413
00:25:59.770 --> 00:26:01.870
[CROCODILE]
You're just a two-bit nobody
who comes from

414
00:26:01.940 --> 00:26:03.140
who-knows-where!

415
00:26:04.840 --> 00:26:06.540
You can't beat me!

416
00:26:06.610 --> 00:26:09.780
Do you have any idea who I am?

417
00:26:09.810 --> 00:26:13.550
I don't care who you are,
'cause it doesn't matter!

418
00:26:13.620 --> 00:26:17.450
Whoever you are, I will beat you!

419
00:26:23.870 --> 00:26:24.900
[CROCODILE growls]

420
00:26:32.940 --> 00:26:35.010
Now fall with this ancient temple,

421
00:26:35.040 --> 00:26:37.250
and let the desert
sands bury you!

422
00:26:38.680 --> 00:26:40.210
Sables...

423
00:26:43.270 --> 00:26:44.980
Hazado!

424
00:26:52.270 --> 00:26:54.100
[LUFFY inhales]

425
00:27:06.650 --> 00:27:10.290
[LUFFY]
Gum-Gum...

426
00:27:11.390 --> 00:27:12.560
[CROCODILE]
Desert...

427
00:27:13.790 --> 00:27:15.490
[LUFFY]
...Storm!

428
00:27:15.530 --> 00:27:17.330
[CROCODILE]
...Spada!

429
00:27:18.460 --> 00:27:23.330
[LUFFY yelling]

430
00:27:33.740 --> 00:27:35.380
[LUFFY grunts]

431
00:27:41.420 --> 00:27:45.160
[LUFFY yelling]

432
00:27:46.990 --> 00:27:52.830
[LUFFY yelling]

433
00:28:28.360 --> 00:28:29.770
Amazing!

434
00:28:29.800 --> 00:28:31.870
He punched him straight
up through the bedrock

435
00:28:31.870 --> 00:28:33.240
beneath the city!

436
00:28:44.240 --> 00:28:45.540
Hey, you guys!

437
00:28:45.570 --> 00:28:46.880
Look there!

438
00:28:55.550 --> 00:28:57.080
[GROUP]
– Crocodile?!
– Crocodile?!

439
00:29:16.000 --> 00:29:17.570
[VIVI]
Now that this
conflict has escalated,

440
00:29:17.600 --> 00:29:19.970
more blood will be shed throughout the kingdom.

441
00:29:20.010 --> 00:29:21.640
We're at war.

442
00:29:21.660 --> 00:29:23.460
[sobs]
You're trying to
get me home safely,

443
00:29:23.500 --> 00:29:24.630
but there's no time!

444
00:29:24.660 --> 00:29:27.060
I need to get home as quickly as possible!

445
00:29:27.100 --> 00:29:28.300
If I don't make it back in time,

446
00:29:28.330 --> 00:29:32.140
a million innocent citizens will
give their lives needlessly!

447
00:29:32.170 --> 00:29:35.310
[crying]

448
00:29:42.370 --> 00:29:44.150
A million innocent citizens will
give their lives needlessly!

449
00:29:44.150 --> 00:29:45.580
[LUFFY]
Right. Well, this should be fun!

450
00:29:45.650 --> 00:29:48.220
All we have to do is beat
up that Crocodile guy!

451
00:29:52.060 --> 00:29:53.090
[VIVI]
Luffy...

452
00:29:55.030 --> 00:29:59.000
[SOLDIERS yelling]

453
00:30:00.330 --> 00:30:02.160
I don't know how he got there in the first place,

454
00:30:02.160 --> 00:30:04.560
but I'm sure it can
only mean one thing.

455
00:30:04.600 --> 00:30:06.090
I knew it! I knew it!

456
00:30:06.090 --> 00:30:08.120
I never doubted it for a second!

457
00:30:09.370 --> 00:30:11.610
It can only mean...

458
00:30:11.610 --> 00:30:14.210
[GROUP]
– Luffy did it! He won!
– Luffy did it! He won!

459
00:30:22.480 --> 00:30:26.580
[VIVI]
Please! Our enemy is defeated.

460
00:30:28.380 --> 00:30:31.250
[SOLDIERS yelling]

461
00:30:32.450 --> 00:30:35.100
[VIVI sobs]

462
00:30:35.100 --> 00:30:37.800
Don't shed any more blood.

463
00:30:37.840 --> 00:30:41.340
[crying]

464
00:30:41.370 --> 00:30:43.310
[VIVI]
Stop fighting!

465
00:30:43.340 --> 00:30:45.780
Please stop fighting!

466
00:31:06.230 --> 00:31:08.230
[KOZA grunts]
[REBEL B]
– Koza!

467
00:31:08.300 --> 00:31:09.870
Hey, are you all right?

468
00:31:13.710 --> 00:31:15.110
[KOZA]
Do you see it?

469
00:31:28.890 --> 00:31:31.090
[TOTO]
Don't be so suspicious, Koza.

470
00:31:38.100 --> 00:31:40.070
[TOTO]
The rain will fall.

471
00:31:50.580 --> 00:31:53.780
[KOZA]
The battle... will end.

472
00:31:58.950 --> 00:32:00.020
[TASHIGI]
Rain.

473
00:32:01.980 --> 00:32:04.820
[SOLDIERS yelling]

474
00:32:11.120 --> 00:32:13.930
[TASHIGI]
The madness has finally stopped.

475
00:32:13.930 --> 00:32:15.460
They're beginning to hesitate.

476
00:32:18.770 --> 00:32:20.930
[CHOPPER]
The rain is starting
to clear the air.

477
00:32:34.250 --> 00:32:35.950
Stop fighting!

478
00:32:37.050 --> 00:32:40.690
Listen to me!

479
00:32:47.090 --> 00:32:49.690
They've heard
Vivi's voice. Finally.

480
00:32:56.200 --> 00:32:57.670
Vivi.

481
00:32:57.700 --> 00:32:59.440
The princess.

482
00:32:59.500 --> 00:33:00.700
Vivi?

483
00:33:00.740 --> 00:33:02.900
I didn't know the
princess had come back.

484
00:33:09.970 --> 00:33:11.640
[ROYAL SOLDIER B]
Sir Crocodile?

485
00:33:11.670 --> 00:33:13.110
[ROYAL SOLDIER C]
How did he get here?

486
00:33:13.110 --> 00:33:15.110
What happened to him?

487
00:33:15.140 --> 00:33:17.980
Oh, so they're still calling him Sir Crocodile?

488
00:33:18.010 --> 00:33:21.010
We'll see if he's Sir Crocodile
after I tell them what's what!

489
00:33:22.110 --> 00:33:24.220
Hold on. Just stay here.

490
00:33:36.770 --> 00:33:39.470
[VIVI]
The rain has returned.

491
00:33:39.540 --> 00:33:42.540
And will fall again,
as it used to.

492
00:33:44.210 --> 00:33:46.380
Our nightmare is over.

493
00:33:46.380 --> 00:33:47.720
Finally over.

494
00:34:09.570 --> 00:34:10.740
I thank you.

495
00:34:20.150 --> 00:34:21.420
No sweat!
